[Desktop Entry]
Type=Application
Name=Input method (disabled by Bashan OS)
Exec=/bin/true
Terminal=false
NoDisplay=true
Hidden=true
X-GNOME-Autostart-enabled=false
# Bashan OS — Stage 9 defect 6.
#
# im-config's autostart launched IBus, which immediately showed a
# notification about Wayland on first boot, to users who had asked for
# nothing.
#
# The filename matters and is NOT a guess: `dpkg -L im-config` shows
# /etc/xdg/autostart/im-launch.desktop. An override under any other name
# does nothing at all, silently. "Hidden=true" in /etc/xdg/autostart is the
# documented way to cancel an autostart entry a package ships, without
# removing the package.
#
# IBus itself stays INSTALLED. All thirteen shipped languages type through
# ordinary keyboard layouts, so nothing needs an input method by default.
# Anyone who does need one - handwriting, pinyin, a script their keyboard
# lacks - turns it on with `im-config` and it starts from then on.
